{
 "_comentario": [
  "El aspecto del EQUIPO DE VERDAD, no de las prendas de apariencia.",
  "",
  "Medido sobre las capturas del servidor de torneos, donde se equipan objetos reales de",
  "uno en uno: ivq dice a que hueco entra el objeto y el lxc siguiente trae el aspecto.",
  "El uid se traduce con el inventario de la captura de entrada al mundo de esa sesion.",
  "",
  "  skins   la pieza mete esa piel en el f6 del personaje",
  "  mounts  monturas y mascoturas, que mandan en la raiz",
  "  pets    mascotas, subentidad del enganche 1",
  "",
  "Para que sirve: hoy el emulador AÑADE la piel de un cosmetico al aspecto en vez de",
  "sustituir la de la pieza que tapa, porque no sabia cual era. Con esta tabla ya se puede",
  "hacer lo que hace el juego.",
  "",
  "Lo genera tools/extraer_equipo_real.py",
  "",
  "=====================================================================",
  "EXTENSION BY IMAGE MATCHING  (inferred, NOT captured)",
  "=====================================================================",
  "",
  "The 286 entries above are measured from real captures. Everything listed",
  "in `_inferred` below was derived offline from the client's own files, with",
  "no server traffic and no Ankama account involved.",
  "",
  "THE IDEA",
  "  A skin bundle (Content/Characters/Skins/skins_assets_skin_<id>.bundle)",
  "  holds the texture of the piece as it is worn. The item icon bundle",
  "  (Content/Picto/Items) holds the same piece drawn as an inventory icon,",
  "  addressed by ItemData.iconId. Two drawings of the same object, so their",
  "  colour signatures line up. That is the whole trick.",
  "",
  "TWO PASSES",
  "  1. RGB histogram 14x14x14 over the opaque pixels at 64x64 picks the eight",
  "     closest skins out of all 5538 bundles.",
  "  2. Those eight are re-scored with a 24x24x24 histogram at 160x160, using",
  "     the 2x icon bundle. At that resolution the details that separate the",
  "     variants of one set survive the resampling; at 64x64 they do not.",
  "  A skin is never assigned twice.",
  "",
  "VALIDATION  (this is the part that matters)",
  "  Run against the 285 measured pairs, searching the full pool of 5538 skins,",
  "  with each item's own answer left in the draw:",
  "     274 correct out of 274 above the confidence margin -> 100% precision,",
  "     96% coverage.",
  "  Also confirmed in game: the pieces render correctly.",
  "",
  "  Two approaches were tried and DROPPED because they measured worse, which",
  "  is worth writing down so nobody repeats them:",
  "     - adding an alpha-silhouette descriptor: 97% precision, and coverage",
  "       fell from 244 to 114 pieces.",
  "     - using the iconId ordering as a prior: same, it degraded the good",
  "       cases. Icon order does correlate with skin order (~85% monotonic)",
  "       but it is locally shuffled, so it cannot be trusted.",
  "",
  "CONFIDENCE  -- the two lists are not the same thing",
  "",
  "  `_inferred`  the best candidate beats the runner-up by more than 0.04.",
  "               This is the validated set described above.",
  "",
  "  `_inferred_needs_review`  below that margin. On the ambiguous cases among",
  "               the known pairs this only lands 36% of the time, so roughly",
  "               two out of three here are expected to be WRONG. They are",
  "               included to reach full coverage, and a few have already been",
  "               reported as visibly off in game. Anyone who would rather draw",
  "               nothing than draw the wrong piece should drop these ids.",
  "               They are the natural target for a real capture pass.",
  "",
  "  Forcing a global one-to-one assignment (Hungarian) over the ambiguous",
  "  cases does not help either: also 36%. There is simply no signal left in",
  "  the image for those.",
  "",
  "Generated by tools/match_skins_by_image.py",
  "Done with Claude (Claude Code)."
 ],
